A trapezium has an area of $27\text{ cm}^2$. Find its perpendicular height $h$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(4,0)--(3,2.25)--(1,2.25)--cycle;
\path (2,0) node[below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\path (2,2.25) node[above] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\draw[->] (0.6,0)--(1.1,0);
\draw[->] (1.3,2.25)--(1.8,2.25);
\draw[dashed] (2.6,0)--(2.6,2.25);
\path (2.6,1.125) node[right] {$h$};
\draw (2.35,0)--(2.35,0.25)--(2.6,0.25);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

This trapezium has an area of $33\text{ m}^2$. Find the length of its parallel side $q$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(0,4)--(2,3)--(2,1)--cycle;
\path (0,2) node[left] {$10\text{ m}$};
\path (2,2) node[right] {$q$};
\draw[->] (0,0.7)--(0,1.2);
\draw[->] (2,1.2)--(2,1.7);
\draw[dashed] (0,2.5)--(2,2.5);
\path (1,2.5) node[above] {$4.4\text{ m}$};
\draw (0,2.25)--(0.25,2.25)--(0.25,2.5);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
